# Docker build-context excludes for backend/Dockerfile (PSY-1790).
#
# WHY IT LIVES HERE, NOT AT THE REPO ROOT. Docker reads `.dockerignore` from
# the root of the build CONTEXT, and both builds of this image use `backend/`
# as the context:
#   * CI      — .github/workflows/backend-image.yml sets `context: ./backend`
#   * Railway — the service's root directory is /backend, and railway.toml's
#               `dockerfilePath = "Dockerfile"` resolves inside it.
# A repo-root .dockerignore would be read by NEITHER, and would fail silently.
#
# DENY-LIST, DELIBERATELY. The builder stage runs `COPY . .` and then
# `go build ./cmd/server`, so the entire Go tree has to arrive. An allow-list
# would silently drop the next package someone adds. For the same reason,
# nothing here excludes `*_test.go` or `testdata/`: `go build` does not need
# them, but `go vet` and `go test` type-check them, so excluding them would
# plant a build-time-only break for whoever later adds a verification stage.
# Measured, that restraint costs 7.24MB of context and buys back ~0.3s.
#
# backend/Dockerfile is the source of truth for what the image needs; do not
# restate its COPY set here. Two constraints are NOT visible from it, and are
# the ones an edit to this file is most likely to break:
#
#   1. internal/services/geo/data/ — ~11MB of TSV reached only through
#      `//go:embed` in geo.go. No COPY names it; excluding it fails the
#      compile, not a COPY.
#   2. db/migrations/ is SQL, so never reach for a blanket `*.sql`.
#
# PATTERN ANCHORING, the other way to break this file. Docker matches with
# filepath.Match semantics, so `*` does NOT cross `/`: a bare `server` matches
# only <context>/server. That is load-bearing for the stray-binary block
# below — `**/server` or `**/main` would delete cmd/server/ and every other
# cmd/ package. Root-anchored names there, `**/` only where stated.
#
# The Backend Image Build check is required on main and runs un-path-filtered
# on every PR, so a mistake here blocks merge rather than reaching Railway.

# Go coverage output. Written by scripts/coverage.sh and by CI's
# `go test -coverprofile=...`; never an input to anything. `coverage.sh`
# rewrites coverage.out on every run, so this also stops a local `COPY . .`
# cache bust per coverage run. If a future golden-file test ever adopts the
# conventional testdata/*.out extension, narrow this rule.
**/*.out
**/coverage.html

# Compiled host-arch binaries left in place by `go build` inside backend/.
# The names mirror the repo .gitignore's PSY-429 and PSY-1550 blocks, plus
# `main` (the Dockerfile's own -o target) and cmd/ targets those blocks miss.
# A darwin/arm64 cmd/server measures 61MB — over twice the whole context —
# and busts `COPY . .` on every rebuild.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. See PATTERN ANCHORING above: adding `**/` to any
# line below would exclude the cmd/ source package of the same name.
main
server
seed
scaffold
scrape-import
discovery-import
backfill-slugs
link-release-labels
openapi-spec
gen-api-token

# Local logs, database dumps, and backups. `backups/` is where every backup
# producer writes (scripts/backup.sh, restore.sh, railway-migrate-*.sh); the
# two `backup_*.tar.gz` / `*_dump_*.sql` patterns match files that are still
# tracked in git at backend/ root, which is where 6.9MB of the measured
# context saving comes from. Untracking those is a separate change: the blobs
# are already in the pack, so only a history rewrite would reclaim them.
logs/
**/*.log
backups/
backup_*.tar.gz
*_dump_*.sql

# Environment files. Nothing reads them at build time. This is a real
# containment boundary and not just hygiene: on main the image job runs
# `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max`, which exports the BUILDER layers — the ones
# `COPY . .` writes — into the shared GitHub Actions cache.
**/.env*

# Local orchestration and host provisioning. Compose brings up dev/e2e/stage
# stacks from OUTSIDE the image, and systemd units target VMs, not containers.
docker-compose*.yml
systemd/

# Docs. Prose only; no build stage reads it. Excluding these is also what
# lets a docs-only PR hit the cached `COPY . .` instead of re-running the
# ~39s Go build in the always-run image job.
docs/
**/*.md

# Editor / OS droppings. `**/` because Finder writes .DS_Store into whatever
# directory it browses, not just the root.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# A locally-installed dependency tree. The layout-deps stage runs its own
# `npm ci` from package.json + package-lock.json, so a host node_modules is
# both unused and (being built for the host arch) wrong.
**/node_modules/
